# Cloudflare Pages redirects for HazardNet.
#
# Format: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# (`from  to  [status]` — the status is optional and defaults to 302.)
#
# This replaced `vercel.json`'s `redirects` array on 2026-10-26, when the
# deployment moved to Cloudflare Pages only (both `hazardnet.live` and
# `www.hazardnet.live` CNAME to `hazardnet.pages.dev`). Cloudflare serves this
# file from the asset root; Vite copies it verbatim into `dist/` because it
# lives in `frontend/public/`.
#
# Deliberately absent: a catch-all `/* /index.html 200` rewrite.
#
# The prerenderer emits a real HTML file per route (frontend/scripts/prerender.mjs),
# so known URLs are files and never need a rewrite. An unknown URL falls to
# `404.html`, which Cloudflare Pages serves automatically with a 404 status and
# which is the *noindex* shell — the page still boots the SPA, so a route that is
# real but unlisted (a profile URL, an alert id) renders for the visitor while a
# crawler is told not to index it. A `/* /index.html 200` rule would undo that:
# every unknown URL would answer 200 with the indexable homepage, which is the
# soft-404 case __tests__/seoFoundations.test.js exists to prevent.

/documentation  /docs  301
